test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:8:15:
  |
8 | Page = Home | Editor (Doc * Mode)
  |               ^
warning: Page.Editor is never reached: neither __init nor any transition that can happen puts the app there

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:15:11:
   |
15 | __pattern Link = App(Link.On)
   |           ^
pattern Link has the name of a type; a pattern's name is new to the spec

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:16:11:
   |
16 | __pattern Max = App(Link.On)
   |           ^
pattern Max has the name of a constant; a pattern's name is new to the spec

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:17:16:
   |
17 | __pattern P(x, x) = App(x)
   |                ^
parameter x is written twice

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:18:16:
   |
18 | __pattern Q(x, y) = App(x)
   |                ^
parameter y is not used in the body of Q

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:19:13:
   |
19 | __pattern R(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc#d * z))
   |             ^
parameter x is not used in the body of R

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:19:38:
   |
19 | __pattern R(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc#d * z))
   |                                      ^
a pattern's body names no value; name it at the use, as an argument

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:19:42:
   |
19 | __pattern R(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc#d * z))
   |                                          ^
z is not a parameter of R; a pattern's body uses only its parameters

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:20:11:
   |
20 | __pattern R = App
   |           ^
pattern R is defined twice (first on line 19)

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:21:44:
   |
21 | __pattern V(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc(Title(x + 1)) * x'))
   |                                            ^
parameter x stands for a whole argument, not a value inside a computed one

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:21:54:
   |
21 | __pattern V(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc(Title(x + 1)) * x'))
   |                                                      ^
parameter x stands for a whole argument; write the prime or the name at the use

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:22:13:
   |
22 | __pattern W(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc(Title(#t)) * Mode))
   |             ^
parameter x is not used in the body of W

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:22:45:
   |
22 | __pattern W(x) = App(Page.Editor(Doc(Title(#t)) * Mode))
   |                                             ^
a pattern's body names no value; name it at the use, as an argument

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:23:11:
   |
23 | __pattern S = T
   |           ^
pattern S uses itself, through T; a pattern may use another, but not in a cycle

test/check/error-pattern-definitions.sumspec:24:11:
   |
24 | __pattern T = U(S)
   |           ^
pattern T uses itself, through S; a pattern may use another, but not in a cycle

